North Korea fired yet another ballistic  missile overnight part of an escalating  series of tests the newest missile was  launched from the country's East Coast  it flew about 280 miles before landing  in the sea off the coast of Japan  the White House says President Trump has  been briefed but has no other comment  Ben Tracy is in Beijing with the rising  tensions in the region  Ben good morning good morning this  missile launch by North Korea appears to  be a short-range ballistic scud missile  in Japan says it could have easily hit  an airplane or a ship in the area so if  anyone thought that pressure from the US  or even China would have slowed down  North Korea's missile test that appears  to be wishful thinking North Korea has  now conducted nine missile launches this  year three in just the past three weeks  the latest comes after the country  claimed its leader Kim jong-un oversaw a  successful test of a new anti-aircraft  system this past weekend Japan was quick  to condemn the new missile launch as  with South Korea whose new president has  said he wants better relations with  North Korea despite international  sanctions North Korea's capabilities  continue to grow  last week the country said it perfected  a medium-range solid-fuel missile that  it would start mass producing and  earlier this month it tested what is  believed to be its longest range missile  yet potentially capable of carrying a  nuclear warhead but still not able to  reach the United States 2014 was the  last time the US tested its West Coast  missile defense system which has only  worked in about half of the trials on  Tuesday the US military will attempt to  shoot down an intercontinental ballistic  missile for the first time the Trump  administration has now sent two aircraft  carriers to the Korean Peninsula but US  defense secretary James Madison unfazed  the nation that a military conflict in  North Korea would be  destruct the North Korean regime has  hundreds of artillery cannons and rocket  launchers within range of one of the  most densely populated cities on earth  which is the capital of South Korea  while North Korea continues these  missile tests it has not conducted a six  nuclear test which many people have  expected when we read North Korea last  month I asked the Vice foreign minister  if they still plan to conduct that test  and he said Kim jong-un will do it  whenever he sees fit  Anthony Ben Tracy thanks
 

